###### Abstract

Herston, Timothy H. M.S., Purdue University, August, 2003. A Study of Phi Meson Yield in 200 GeV/A Au+Au Collisions at RHIC. Major Professors: Andrew Hirsch, Rolf Scharenberg, and Fuqiang Wang.

Herein is reported the results of phi meson yields in Au+Au collisions at \(\sqrt{s_{NN}}\)=200 GeV and measurement of the mean value and width of the phi resonance peak at different centralities. The yields were largely in agreement with previous studies using different analysis methodology. No changes in the phi mass peak's mean value or width were observed.

